A||||90||DecadenceR||Nascar... is it a sport?||||1||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||08-17-2001||11:37 AM||||I got into an argument about this last night with a girl. While I believe that all the Nascar drivers are brave and talented, I don't believe that it's a sport, and I don't think that the drivers are athletes. It DOES take good reflexes and quick thinking, but as long as you can fit into the car you don't have to do much in the way of physical training for this. <BR>And since I got her to stop talking to me for tbe evening with this argument, I thought I'd see what you all have to say.||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||08-17-2001||11:49 AM||||if you think it takes no physical training, lets see you sit in a bare bones car for 4 1/2 hours, in 109 degrees, traveling at 200+ miles an hour - then we will see what your opinions are||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-17-2001||11:50 AM||||"There are only three true sports:  mountain climbing, bull fighting, and motor racing.  The rest are all games."<P>--Ernest Hemingway||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||08-17-2001||11:52 AM||||NO it is show-biz and like the WWF it is a pre-planed fix.<P>and when will they build a rear drive V-8 like they race   ????      never.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||08-17-2001||12:00 PM||||This is one of the chapters in 'How to Win freinds and influence people'<P> you can win an argument, and in the process, lose a friend.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-17-2001||12:33 PM||||isnt the definition of sport 'competition between indivduals demontrating athletic prowness' technicaly then motor racing is not. however who calls fishing and golf sports? When did someone think using a camera to follow a tiny ball thru the air exciting. If anyone should get the award, its the camera operator to be able to track it. at least in racing there is some degree of excitement most of the time. I been for rules making them use stock production cars for year with the obvious exception of using the current nascar frame/rollcage. what happened to the old rule of manufacturer had to sell so many of a car before it was allowed to race? Thats why I now watch more GT and touring car races, there really mostly production cars modified to race. most of them still have original inst panel and most of the interior even.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||08-17-2001||01:58 PM||||I agree with c m west and Chadman...<P>I doubt that there are many here who could take the rigors of a 500 mile NASCAR race.<P>And fixed? Please! I wonder how they talked Earnhardt into waiting till the last lap to crash and kill himself.<P>And danger, Ken? There are more ex-football players sitting around in wheelchairs than there are ex-NASCAR drivers. Sure accidents happen, but that happens in any <B>SPORT</B>. No matter what sport (or anything else) someone is in, they know the risks and decide to go for it...<P>Now Roger.. how about Webster's definition of a sport?<P><B>sport</B> n. 1. An amusing or interesting pastime: diversion. 2. A physical activity, esp. one with a set of rules.<P>There are other definitions but they relate to joking and showing off...<P>I challenge anyone to say that NASCAR does not fit into Webster's definition of sport. If you think it isn't physical... just try it! And please don't judge something that you don't even watch. You have to try anything before making a sound judgement on it.<P>To borrow from another thread.. NASCAR isn't just a bunch of redneck fuk's driving real fast in circles anymore. It is technology and the rules are there to make it competitive and keep people alive.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||08-17-2001||02:24 PM||||Sure it's a sport. Nascar racing is very demanding, physically. Those guys gave got to be in shape. When is the last time you saw a fat Nascar driver?<P>I agree with Roger, though. I think they need to go back to racing cars that are based on production cars. <P>And rayb... I've read that rear wheel drive is slowly making a comeback in the automotive industry. <BR>Maybe you'll get your (our) wish. <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ray b||08-17-2001||03:24 PM||||the nasty cars were real back in 60'70's but not for last ten or more years.<BR>i wish they would run real cars now like euro-cars and japs high end cars againts mark 7 or N* but old rules that limit the motors to push-rods suck, carbs who still used a carb in the last 20 years.<BR>both GM and mopar have no rear drives and ford only use front drive in theirs that race<BR>so there is no carry over to the street at least in the old days if you ran a 427 you had to sell them to all who would pay the price, not now.<BR>then there is the fix problem like little E's win!!!??? sure looked like he had some thing going on in that race. are all the races fixed no just the ones that someone gets THE CALL.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000009||frontal lobe||08-17-2001||03:27 PM||||They have done monitoring of drivers during the race.  Heart rates are usually sustained in the 140's and often peak in the 180's.  Same for the formula 1 and indy car guys.  Lot's of strain on the old ticker.  Physically more demanding than one would think.<P>Who was complaining recently about that new Chicago race track where the g-force was so severe that guys were losing blood to the brain and getting dizzy and almost passing out, and so they canceled the race.  No, wait, it was Arlington Texas where they canceled the race, right?<P>Whether or not is a sport is largely semantics.  I do admire the concentration and skill involved.  Just don't like the contrived nature of FORCING it to be competitive (like the stupid eliminating of leads and bunching cars again after a yellow just to FORCE it to be close).<P>I REALLY admire the COURAGE of the drivers, especially Mark Martin's courage for driving HIS car!  Anybody know what I'm getting at?||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||08-17-2001||03:30 PM||||"Mountain climbing, bull fighting, and motor racing are the only real sports, the rest are merely games."<P>--Ernest Hemingway<P>That said, Indy and Formula 1 are *racing* nascar is IMO rather silly.<P>But it's still a sport, and if you think it takes no physical conditioning, well, try it sometime :)<P>They had to cancel (imo a bad decision, but that's an unqualified opinion) an Indy CART race, because the cars were toooo fast on the track.  Think the drivers are wussies?  How much do you weigh? I weigh 165lbs.<P>If I had to race with over NINE HUNDRED AND SEVEN pounds of weight pushing my lungs shut, I would pull the race too.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||Songman||08-17-2001||03:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>then there is the fix problem like little E's win!!!??? sure looked like he had some thing going on in that race. are all the races fixed no just the ones that someone gets THE CALL. [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah.. it was plain to see that that race was fixed. Dale Jr never has been a good driver. And it was obvious that everyone just slowed down in the last few laps to let him get up there and he just didn't have a dominant car all day long. (How do you show sarcasm on this thing?!?) There are always gonna be whiny babies (either drivers or fans) that don't like the outcome of a race and will yell foul. Something else in common with every other <B>sport</B>. Not calling you a whiny baby, just talking in general. I have no idea who you pull for.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>I REALLY admire the COURAGE of the drivers, especially Mark Martin's courage for driving HIS car!  Anybody know what I'm getting at?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, I know exactly what you mean there! hehe<BR>But if he didn't have the courage I am sure that his sponsor would help him 'get it up', so to speak... HAHAH<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000012||Cooter||08-17-2001||03:41 PM||||After driving for a couple of seasons of kart racing, I can honestly tell you that it takes a very athletic person to handle the physical demands of driving the car. Why else would they have dedicated physical trainers, exercise and weight programs for the drivers and crew? I was fairly fit, but after a night of racing, I felt like I had run in a marathon! Anytime you have that level of competition, whether it is man Vs. man or man/machince vs. man/machine it is a sport.||||reg||1
Z||000013||rogergarrison||08-17-2001||04:42 PM||||songman, you may have misunderstood some of what I said. I love stock car racing, I did it myself for years. When it was really racing and not just advertising. I did lots of my own mechanic work, paid for lots myself, even drove the hauler to get to the track. I had lots of fun, no big wigs telling me what to do, my 'fancy'driver suit was full of grease spots (ask lisa, shes got it for coveralls) I just think its gotten to corperate driven too much. So I know how much it takes to 'just drive' i was so tired and worn out, sore sometimes couldnt get out of bed next morning. Make em back to some semblence of 'stock cars' and Ill luv it again. <P>No I dont think any race is 'fixed'. It would be way too hard, there are way too many variables. How do you know the guy thats supposed to win isnt gonna blow a tire in the last minutes, or an engine. Im sure everyone races to win.||||reg||1
Z||000014||GarethWright||08-17-2001||04:57 PM||||Nascar Directions to Finish Line:<BR>Take first left, go straight, turn left, go straight, turn left, go straight, turn left go straight.  Repeat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Nascar isnt a sport, its a sleep-aid, unless you are DRIVING the car, then its hard work.<BR>As watching televised motorsport goes, I'll take Rally or Formula1 over Nascar any day.<BR>In Formula you get to see Right turns too, and in Rally, cars fly, and thats just plain kewl.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
