Z||000018||Songman||08-17-2001||10:49 PM||||I have an idea.. let's just take humans out of everything! We can build robot football players! That would be fun. And that way no one gets hurt. Let's even replace all of your jobs with computers and robots too. I'm sure you would all love that just as much as NASCAR drivers would love your suggestion to take them out of the cars. This sort of reminds me of other arguments here... if you don't like it, no one should be allowed to do it.<P>Did anyone happen to see where I posted Webster's definition of sport? Just being a physical activity doesn't make it a sport. An organized physical activity with a set of rules for the competitor however is a sport. <P>And Roger, by posting the Webster's definition I didn't have a problem with anything you said. Just that Webster's is the accepted standard for definitions just about anywhere you go. And I know all about the advertising budget for NASCAR. I'll post a couple of pictures of one of my friends that stays at my house when he comes through Nashville. I am a NASCAR fan (apparently this means I can stay awake through a race.) and am glad that NASCAR and country music are so closely tied so I can know some of these guys. Obviously these pictures were last year because of the paint scheme.<P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dj88.jpg">      <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dj88a.jpg">     <BR>And yes, I know my legs are white! That is not the point of the pictures! hehe <P>And here is one to go with yours DXR_DAD. One of my truck buddies... well, me in his truck anyway. Taken the night before the Craftsman Truck Series race in Nashville the next day... and he won too!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gb7truck.jpg">   <P>Anyway... the fact that there is such a huge budget for these cars is another reason the races aren't fixed. Some of these teams lose money every year. The cost of getting into NASCAR is astronomical. So why would these teams be there if the races were fixed and they knew they were gonna lose money?<P>Plus... I think you'll find an awful lot of NASCAR fans disagree with you about whether or not this is a sport and whether or not it is boring. No other sport brings in the crowds nor the prices per ticket as NASCAR. Talk about baseball or football all you want, but I think NASCAR is America's sport these days. Go to a race and be prepared to have your mind's changed. I used to think just like a lot of you do before I knew what it was all about.<P>And don't anybody think I am mad.. I'm just giving an informed opinion. But I am often amazed at some of the comparisons that people come up with to try to prove their points! hehe.. I agree that football players don't drive race cars to stay in shape, nor does anyone go play professional football to 'stay' in shape. You are in shape before you go there in both instances.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">      <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
