Z||000037||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||09:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>Vice Grips as anything is a sport.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It takes talent to drive a Winston Cup car, if it didn't then why isn't everyone doing it? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ez.....not everyone has a couple of million dollars lying around. <P>and while were talking skill, what about drag racing, how much skill to go straight for a 1/4 mile with the gas on the floor. With a good wheel alighment, a car can do that by itself with a brick on the pedal.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000038||Songman||08-19-2001||10:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B> ez.....not everyone has a couple of million dollars lying around. <P>and while were talking skill, what about drag racing, how much skill to go straight for a 1/4 mile with the gas on the floor. With a good wheel alighment, a car can do that by itself with a brick on the pedal.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The first part of this helps prove why NASCAR isn't fixed. Why would the teams that don't end in front and make the big bucks show up if it was? Lots of these teams lose money year after year just hoping that this next year will be the year when they get the breaks.<P>As for the second part.. it takes a helluva lot of skill. I couldn't do it. Not at the speeds they do. And have you seen the horrific fireball crashes? Guess the car forgot to go straight, huh? I'm not a big fan of drag racing either, but I do know that there is a lot of skill involved.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
