Z||000040||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||10:34 AM||||songman, seems like were always at odds. I tried the drag racing stuff when i was a kid. like nascar it was fun in the old days. everyone raced cars in thier own class. like all 289/283 sticks, all 350/351 autos. when they started that ET bracket (i think thats what its called) it got silly. i pull to the line with a 273 barracuda and have to race a 427 chevy. sure i get a big head start. i rather see heads up starts between cars may the best car win. throw away the goofy 'christmas tree' just have a 'ready and go' lite.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>oh im pretty sure that most wrecks in drag races are not driver errors. could be wrong since i dont watch em anymore, but i think its usually cause something breaks.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
