Z||000050||bHooper||08-19-2001||10:28 PM||||ok, i found and interesting web site for the so called "international race of champions" <A HREF="http://www.irocracing.com/current_season/history.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.irocracing.com/current_season/history.html</A> <P>i find it hard to call this an "international race of champions" any more, since all they do is race in spec nascars around an oval track.  at one time (back in the '70s) they invited drivers from all over, to race on all types of surface's.  in the mid '80s they started their process of fazing out the road racers, by inviting the older "over the hill gang" of john watson, and people like that.  in fact the last F1 driver was martin brundle (hardly a champion, but an average number 2 man).<P>its hard to call a series "the international race of champions" when they don't race on different racing surfaces (i.e... temporary and permanent road course, small and big ovals) or invite drivers from other series (come on a washed up al unser doesnt count) or race in other countries (heck canada counts as another country, and they have some beautifull road (oops thats a naughty word isnt it?) courses!)<P>anyway, they have a long way to go b4 it's a race of champions again... the '70s were great, but unfortunatly the wrong people have hold of it now!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000051||fiero56||08-19-2001||11:52 PM||||<B>NASCAR: Non Athletic Sport Centered Around Rednecks </B><P>First I have to say its been a while since I read something so funny on the forum that I burst out laughing. But this is one of the rare few.<P>I am always surprised when I see how many people follow these events. I'll admit I know very little about nascar(all I learned about nascar I learned watching 20 minutes of one of their sunday morning shows about the sport/game.<P>Seems to me they should just give everyone identical cars and all the teams have to do is do their paint thing. They have so many rules it sounds like the cars might as well all roll off an assembly line.<P>And I too, think if it looks like a (insert model here), they should be driving a (insert model here), not a (insert model here) body on a race-car.<P>I watch open wheel racing on really boring Sunday afternoons, but thats just because the sound of those engines is incredible. If I want to hear a v-8 roaring, all I need to do is find the nearest f-body.||||reg||1
Z||000052||ray b||08-20-2001||12:37 AM||||what about indy layout 4 corners that the bush boys can't drive at all so they go to a small oval to race instead.<BR>homestead was a indy copy i saw cart run on it at over 200 mph but nasty car said rip out the corners and replace with high banked sweepers that the car is set up to turn on hands off wheel and only steer on the straits<BR>that must take alot of skill to drive on the straits like that.<BR>why has no driver ever moved up fron nasty cars to cart or irl but indy guys can win nascar races like aj or p jones or m andreti<BR>ever see tiny lund??? 300lbs and a winner.<BR>why does everybody  know what the call is if they don't make them??<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000053||Songman||08-20-2001||02:06 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>what about indy layout 4 corners that the bush boys can't drive at all so they go to a small oval to race instead.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Some things don't even warrant a reply but I find myself replying anyway... First off, we're talking NASCAR, not <B>BUSCH</B>. Second, what the hell are you talking about?<P><B>homestead was a indy copy i saw cart run on it at over 200 mph but nasty car said rip out the corners and replace with high banked sweepers that the car is set up to turn on hands off wheel and only steer on the straits<BR>that must take alot of skill to drive on the straits like that.</B><P>NASCAR was running at over 200mph too and the officials decided to slow it down. Lots of fans still don't agree with it but that's the breaks. And obviously the people who own/run Homestead thought they could do better on a banked track. Guess more people like that stuff. And you think the cars drive themselves through the turns... as so many of us have said before... try it! I'll be up there with a sponge to scrape you off of the wall. Then if you live, try it with 42 more guys out there...<P><BR><B>why has no driver ever moved up fron nasty cars to cart or irl but indy guys can win nascar races like aj or p jones or m andreti</B><P>If you want to impress us that you know what you are talking about learn to spell. And then tell me why so many of those other guys keep coming to race NASCAR. NASCAR is top of the heap. No one wants to go the other way. it is not that they can't.<P><B>ever see tiny lund??? 300lbs and a winner.</B><P>Typical... pick a name from the 1950s to prove a point! hahah<P><B>why does everybody  know what the call is if they don't make them??</B><P>Again... what the hell are you talking about?!?<P>This is getting old. Answering the same old things over and over.. Get your history books out. NASCAR turned 50 a few years ago. And it gets bigger every year. My last comment on this is that if you aren't seeing what it's about it is your loss.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000054||Pontiaddict||08-20-2001||02:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B> ez.....not everyone has a couple of million dollars lying around.</B> <BR>Well, then they should just put supermodels in the cars so the sponsers can just sell T&A since it doesn't take skill to drive the cars competitively.<P><B>and while were talking skill, what about drag racing, how much skill to go straight for a 1/4 mile with the gas on the floor. With a good wheel alighment, a car can do that by itself with a brick on the pedal.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bracket racing is set up so any idiot with a halfway decent car can pay to run down the track, but it does take skill to run an actual race car. Tell me that any idiot can drive a top fueler and be competitive running next to an actual racer.<P>6 year olds play baseball  and anyone who can run can do it while carrying a football. But put them up against professionals and what do you have?||||reg||1
Z||000055||Galen||08-20-2001||08:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>Galen... I have to say this... I have often wondered if you've ever left the county you were born in?<P>Because sometimes you say and do things that make me think you have lived your whole life within a 3 mile radious.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>May not be alot to do in Richmond County.. but its home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> for now atleast, I've always wanted to go visit some monks and just sit and have long in-depth talks about life and the world. Call me crazy but I like things like that. <P>.. rayb, I normally tend to stay away from your stupidity. But there be plenty of us hicks on this here board, I'd watch who I call a hick  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>.. Songman, we're talking NASCAR, more importantly Winston Cup. Since BGN racing is NASCAR. <P>.. Open ye mouth and be proved an idiot, or keep it shut and just look like one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> that is directed at no one in particular, and no, I wasn't saying that to you rayb<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
