Z||000071||Songman||08-22-2001||09:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hartz:<BR><B>Yo Songman - you going to Bristol this weekend?<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nah, I'm pretty much stuck in town until this CD is done... unless I get to sneak out for Fiero events anyway! hehe<P>Bristol is one track I have never been to, but it is always exciting! Remember when Michael Waltrip hit the gate that was in the middle of turns one and two in the race Busch race and tore his car completely in half? I have that on video tape and if you go frame by frame you can see that the car split right in front of his seat and his legs are sticking straight out over the pavement. Lucky they didn't catch and get pulled back under the car! But he raced in the NASCAR race the next day! Even since they redesigned the track and put in a tunnel to get rid of the gate you can still plan on a lot of wrecks at Bristol.<P>You going?||||reg||7
