Z||000089||FieroKyle||08-23-2001||04:04 AM||||Well, I wish they would run totally stock, I mean fresh off the line. Slap stickers and a racing seat and go with it that way. Run factory engines with no mods, no computer tinking. But in that case, the Grand Prix GTP would always win with its supercharged 3800 V-6 running I think 260 HP, the Monte Carlo SS 2nd with the 3800 V-6 running 200 HP, Dodge Intrepid R/T with its V-6 which I think has like 160 to 190 HP, and the the slow ass Taurus which Ford would be embarrassed to run in a distant 4th. And if that happened, watch GM really make some street cars since they are in competition with the other Big 2. It wouldn't be about cutting corners, just all out stock performance. I could swear though GM made a Monte Carlo model when they came out with their latest redesign call Intimidator. It was a Monte Carlo with two seats, a roll cage, and a 350 sbc in it and it look like a regular lowered monte carlo SS on the oustide, and in it was all racing stuff with a couple actual car items like radio and stuff. It was street legal and everything and they came with Dale Earnhardts signature in the dash. But it was also like race preped with a Simpson racing harness and everything. I wondered what happened with it. I saw one at the Detroit auto show.||||reg||1
